From b90d52d9f01a0ec656f182154311119ff21086fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Miures Manager <contact@miures.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:11:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Media consolidation: Insert media for the question text,
 option image pop-up (1-10-26 review)

- Option Image URL: Choose / Upload open a Customize image pop-up (width,
  height, scale, fit, alignment, proportions, padding, spacing, alt text,
  live preview); nothing reaches the option until Apply. Customize reopens
  it. Stored as option.imageDisplay and applied at every option-image site.
- The separate "Media shown under the question text" field is retired.
  Insert media in the question text now has sources (library, upload, URL,
  Google Drive + save to library), Above / Below / at the cursor, several
  items each with their own settings, YouTube / Vimeo / Drive players and a
  live preview. Old questions keep their media and can move it into the
  text. Position and several items are offered only in the question text.
- Fix: an edited picture was read back as kind "img", so the dialog had no
  preview, no alt field and showed player controls; the preview now
  follows every change.
- Clearing the source of an edited item and pressing Apply removes it.
- Piped image URLs: a {{ImageURL}} source can be inserted; option and
  question media URLs are no longer HTML-escaped (& survived as &amp;);
  a picture whose piped source is empty is dropped.
- POST /api/surveys/[id]/media/import saves a Drive file into the library
  (node-only helpers in @rescript/media/server).
- MediaDisplay gains padding and spacing.

Tests: engine mediaConsolidation (7), media importRemote (4), browser
media-consolidation (14 checks); mutation-checked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAcfUsJLu3R4pYxzaj9SU4
